    "raw": "{\"ruleId\":\"item-248c423fbc2d\",\"class\":\"partial\",\"constraints\":[{\"id\":\"short-keyset-id-in-keys-path\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"/v1/keys/01[0-9a-fA-F]{14}(?![0-9a-fA-F])\",\"path\":\".floor/added/**\"},{\"id\":\"short-keyset-id-literal-in-id-field\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\bid[\\\"']?\\\\s*[:=]\\\\s*[\\\"'`]01[0-9a-fA-F]{14}[\\\"'`]\",\"path\":\".floor/added/**\"}],\"coverage\":\"Added lines that hard-code a short v2 keyset id (\\\"01\\\" followed by exactly 14 hex digits, 16 hex in total) in two places: a /v1/keys/{id} path, or a literal assigned to an `id` field such as BlindedMessage.id or Proof.id.\",\"residual\":\"Does the hunk build a mint request that sends a short (8-byte / 16-hex) keyset id, for example in BlindedMessage.id, Proof.id or a /v1/keys/{keyset_id} path, where the id is not a hard-coded literal (for example a variable holding a truncated or short id)?\",\"probes\":{\"violating\":[{\"patch\":\"--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/wallet/mint-keys.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\\n+export async function loadKeys() {\\n+  return fetch(\\\"https://mint.example.com/v1/keys/01a2b3c4d5e6f7a8\\\");\\n+}\\n\"},{\"patch\":\"--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/wallet/blind.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\\n+export function makeMessage(B_: string) {\\n+  return { amount: 8, id: \\\"01a2b3c4d5e6f7a8\\\", B_ };\\n+}\\n\"}],\"compliant\":{\"patch\":\"--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/wallet/mint-ok.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\\n+export async function loadKeys() {\\n+  return fetch(\\\"https://mint.example.com/v1/keys/01a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9\\\");\\n+}\\n+export function makeMessage(B_: string) {\\n+  return { amount: 8, id: \\\"01a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9\\\", B_ };\\n+}\\n\"}},\"rationale\":\"A hard-coded short v2 keyset id (\\\"01\\\" plus 14 hex) in a keys path or in an id field is a literal pattern that can be checked line by line. Ids that come from variables or truncation, and whether the code actually builds mint requests, need data-flow and semantic judgement. Legacy \\\"00\\\" 16-hex ids are full ids and are excluded.\"}",
